# REQUIRES: uv
# The family-emitted vocabulary crosses the cross-implementation gate:
# both parsers load the value-faithful family's own vocabulary — the
# minted predicate specs with their fail-closed digest keys, the
# instance-baked check contracts, the counted attachment kinds — and
# re-emit it canonically, byte for byte. Until this gate, the generated
# vocabulary's refusal surface sealed on the C++ leg alone.

# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: zkc-family %S/../Oir/Inputs/plonky3-fri-vf.json --emit-vocabulary=%t/vocab.json --emit-spine=%t/spine.mlir
# RUN: zkc-registry-lint %t/vocab.json > %t/vocab.zkc
# RUN: %uv python -m oracle.parity vocabulary-file %t/vocab.json > %t/vocab.oracle
# RUN: diff %t/vocab.zkc %t/vocab.oracle
